     * Solves the problem by calculating the number of open and close parenthesis and then returns the difference between them, which is the minimum number of insertion operations.
     *
     * @param s The input string.
     * @return The minimum number of insertion operations required to make the string balanced.
     */
    public int minInsertions(String s) {
        int open = 0, close = 0;

        // Count the number of open and close parentheses
        for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {
            if (c == '(') {
                // Increment the number of open parentheses
                open++;
            } else {
                // Decrement the number of close parentheses
                close++;
            }
        }

        // Return the difference between the number of open and close parentheses
        return Math.abs(open - close);
    }
